file is unreadable\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt containing the full project context, task description (Task 5575: implement cmd/who core functionality srd097 R1.1-R1.4), execution constitution, coding standards, constraints, and acceptance criteria.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — instructing me to produce a summary instead of continuing implementation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/who/main.go` implementing:\n     - R1.1: Default user listing from utmpx with proper GNU who output format\n     - R1.2: FILE argument support for custom utmpx database\n     - R1.3: \"who am i\" / \"who am I\" support (current terminal only)\n     - R1.4: Exit 1 on utmpx read errors\n   - Run `go build -o bin/who ./cmd/who/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/who/` to verify no warnings (AC2)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two reference files (srd097-who.yaml and cmd/users/main.go) and was about to start implementing `cmd/who/main.go`. I had gathered all the information needed:\n   - The SRD requirements R1.1-R1.4\n   - The CGo utmpx pattern from cmd/users\n   - The design decisions (D1: SIGPIPE handler, D2: utmpx pattern from cmd/users, D3: gwho reference binary)\n   - The file to create: `cmd/who/main.go`\n\n   No code had been written yet. The implementation phase was about to begin.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/who/main.go` using the CGo utmpx pattern from `cmd/users/main.go`, implementing R1.1 (default listing with name/terminal/time/host), R1.2 (FILE argument via `C.utmpxname`), R1.3 (\"who am i\" via current tty matching), and R1.4 (exit 1 on errors). Then verify with `go build -o bin/who ./cmd/who/` and `go vet ./cmd/who/`.\n\n   Key implementation details to remember:\n   - GNU who output format uses specific column widths/alignment\n   - Need `C.GoString(&entry.ut_line[0])` for terminal name\n   - Need `C.GoString(&entry.ut_host[0]